  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "dwg_decode_LWPOLYLINE_private",
    "file": "libredwg/src/dwg.spec",
    "description": "Heap-buffer-overflow read in LWPOLYLINE decoding: the decoder reads the points array via FIELD_2DD_VECTOR(points, num_points, 10) without verifying enough remaining input bytes for num_points elements. With crafted/truncated object data, num_points is accepted but the bitstream ends exactly at/just before the needed point payload, so the vector reader performs a 1-byte read past the heap-backed fuzz input buffer.",
    "conditions": "In llvmfuzz, attacker-controlled DWG bytes reach dwg_decode->decode_R13_R2000->dwg_decode_add_object->dwg_decode_LWPOLYLINE. The PoV must parse as a LWPOLYLINE (R2000+ path) with a nonzero num_points (within existing bound <=20000) so IF_FREE_OR_SINCE(R_2000) executes FIELD_2DD_VECTOR. The object payload is truncated/inconsistent versus num_points, causing out-of-bounds read from the input buffer during point-vector decoding."
  },
